#lang saffron
; saffron-match-any-scrutinee-on-parametric-adt-emits-bad-c: matching an
; unannotated (`any`) scrutinee against a PARAMETRIC ADT.
;
; This emitted uncompilable C -- `aggregate value used where an integer was
; expected`, the 16-byte tagged box cast straight to a pointer -- while the
; non-parametric shape worked. It cost the dialect its headline property on
; user ADTs: in Saffron a parameter is unannotated by design, and here it
; could not be.
;
; The fix is two halves that only work together, which is why relaxing the
; narrow alone was tried and reverted:
;   1. a parametric ctor call BUILDS at `any` in a Saffron file, so `(Sq 6)`
;      is a `(Shape any)` -- the same answer S6 gives container literals;
;   2. the `any`-scrutinee narrow targets the ADT applied to `any`, instead of
;      declining outright on `n_type_params == 0`.
;
; Half 1 alone leaves the C error; half 2 alone compiles and then panics
; `cast: any holds a different instantiation of Shape`.
;
; `w` is used TWICE on purpose. The arm binder inherits the type argument, and
; building that argument with a zeroed Type made it CK_UNIQUE (`CK_MOVE` is an
; alias for it, and it is 0), so the second `w` was a TUR-E0005 use-after-move
; -- while the same `any` as a PARAMETER was fine. One use would not show it.

(defdata Shape [a] (Sq a))

(defn area [s]
  (match s
    (Sq w) (* w w)))

; A ctor field that is NOT a type variable keeps its declared type: the widen
; must not erase an annotation the author wrote.
(defdata Tagged [a] (T :int a))

(defn tag-of [v]
  (match v
    (T n x) (+ n x)))

; The non-parametric shape, which always worked -- here so a "fix" cannot
; regress it while making the parametric one pass.
(defdata Plain (P :int))

(defn plain-of [p]
  (match p
    (P n) (* n 2)))

(defn main []
  (println (cast (area (Sq 6)) int))
  (println (cast (tag-of (T 10 5)) int))
  (println (cast (plain-of (P 21)) int))
  0)
